          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Visit a doctor and find out what happens in ligament rupture, cartilage rupture and fracture of bones. How can we reduce the risk by changing our lifestyle and nutritional balance?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.213,
            0.416,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Perform the following activity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.234,
            0.493,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Sit with your feet flat on the floor."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.251,
            0.607,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Place your fingers on the back of your ankle just above the heel (Fig. 3.24)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.285,
            0.607,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Point your toes down and up, and you will feel the tendon moving."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.318,
            0.609,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Tendons are designed to withstand huge pulling forces. Try exploring other tendons in your body around the different joints."
            }
          ]
        },
