        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.424,
            0.775,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reflect on any gardening methods you know, such as pruning, grafting, irrigation or crop rotation. How does each practice support the healthy functioning of plant tissues like meristems, conducting tissues or supporting tissues?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.495,
            0.526,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Turn a nature walk into a research project."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.516,
            0.773,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Observe different leaves and study their adaptations for various environments, such as desert, very moist or aquatic habitats."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.55,
            0.775,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Consult an elder community resource persons about their knowledge on different plant leaves, such as leaves that remain fresh for a long time, repel water or deter insects. Find out their traditional uses, such as making plates, preparing cooling wraps or functioning as insect repellents."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.635,
            0.775,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y Study various dance forms of different tribal communities across the country. Each student learn and experience at least five steps. Observe the joint movements involved in performing these steps and then develop a dance or drama on the concept of joint movements. Perform this at the school’s annual function so that students from different grades can learn from it."
            }
          ]
        },
